================================================================================================================
SUMMARY
================================================================================================================
  Question (B): does filament-fed spin change retention?  No, not at any level the gates can see.
  - Centrifugal support at lambda' <= 0.05: 66.7% of the support; the density at r_F drops <= 66.5%; r_F stays 12.7-44x
    above threshold; the conversion edge moves <= 33.3% (B1).
  - The vortex lattice: spacing >= 10 pc, filling <= 2e-06, a
    <= 3e-05 polarisation of the random node tangle (B2).
  - Escape: single daughters split prograde/retrograde by up to +0.483, but each pair has one of each, and the pair-averaged
    retention moves by <= 0.0748 (X-COP margin 0.088), the 50% transition by <= 4.2% (B3); at r_F by <= 0.0257 (B4).

  checks: 2/5 pass; load-bearing failures: 3   [15s]
